# Seireiki Rayblade (PS1) English table: source text (ASCII) -> the game's 1-byte and 2-byte glyph codes.
# Letters, digits and a few symbols use the cells the Japanese font already has (8x16 half-width, codes 01-3F and
# 0x100-0x10B); the punctuation below 0x114+ is drawn by tools/font_en.py into blank cells (docs/fonts.md).
# Write a space as \s. Control codes match tbl/jp.tbl, so en text can carry the same {nl}/{page}/{wait}.
